---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Ownership & Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="Who runs Make AI Games, how it makes money, and why that never changes a ranking."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Disclosure', href: '/disclosure' }]}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Ownership and affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <div class="answer">
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is run by {SITE.owner}, which makes <a href="/tools/makko-ai">Makko</a>, one of the tools we
        rank. Makko is scored by the same public rubric and data rules as every other tool, and it is labeled
        wherever it appears.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How the site makes money</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Affiliate links.</strong> Some "Visit" links pay us a commission if you subscribe. They're marked
        "Affiliate link" and use <code>rel="sponsored"</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sponsored placements.</strong> Vendors can pay for a labeled sponsored slot. Sponsorship never changes
        a tool's score or rank.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Makko signups.</strong> When Makko fits what you're looking for, we say so, with this disclosure
        attached.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What money can't buy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A higher score. Scores are computed from facts with <a href="/methodology">published weights</a>.</li>
      <li>Removal of a competitor, or a hidden fact.</li>
      <li>An "Editor's pick" badge. We don't have one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a fact about your tool is wrong or out of date, open an issue or pull request in our public repository with a
      link to a primary source, and we'll update it.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
